// test-error
// Issue #1183 review, round 2: the rule enumerated which expression FORMS are
// Boolean, so anything it did not recognize defaulted to permitted. A
// bool-returning call was unresolvable, and reached the binary:
//     uint8_t c = n / isReady();   ->  SIGFPE, exit 136
//
// Resolved through CodeGenState.getFunctionReturnType, keyed by transpiled C
// name via QualifiedCName -- the single encoder -- so the bare, scope-qualified
// and this.member() spellings all resolve to the same answer.
bool isReady() {
    return false;
}
u8 n <- 10;

void main() {
    u8 c <- n / isReady(); // E0807: divide by zero at runtime
}
